{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Isma'il, Son of Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.)",
  "data": "At the grave of Isma'il, son of Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), in al-Baqi, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى جَدِّكَ الْمُصْطَفٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA JADDIKAL MUSTAFAA\nPeace be upon your forefather, the Chosen One.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَبِيْكَ الْمُرْتَضَى الرِّضَا\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA ABEEKAL MURTADAR RIDAA\nPeace be upon your father Ali al-Murtada, the one well pleased.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى السَّيِّدَيْنِ الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAS SAYYIDAYNIL HASANI WAL HUSAYN\nPeace be upon the two masters, al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى خَدِيْجَةَ اُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA KHADEEJATA UMMIL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon Khadijah, mother of the believers,\nاُمِّ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nUMMI SAYYIDATI NISAA'IL A'ALAMEEN\nmother of the mistress of the women of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى فَاطِمَةَ اُمِّ الْاَئِمَّةِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA FAATIMATA UMMIL A'IMMATIT TAAHIREEN\nPeace be upon Fatimah, mother of the pure Imams.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى النُّفُوْسِ الْفَاخِرَةِ بُحُوْرِ الْعُلُوْمِ الزَّاخِرَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAN NUFOOSIL FAAKHIRATI BUHOORIL U'LOOMIZ ZAAKHIRAH\nPeace be upon the noble souls, the brimming oceans of knowledge,\nشُفَعَاۤئِيْ فِي الْاٰخِرَةِ وَاَوْلِيَاۤئِيْ عِنْدَ عَوْدِ الرُّوْحِ\nSHUFA'AA'EE FIL AAKHIRATI WA AWLIYAA'EE I'NDA A'WDIR ROOH\nmy intercessors in the Hereafter and my guardians when the soul returns\nاِلَى الْعِظَامِ النَّخِرَةِ اَئِمَّةِ الْخَلْقِ وَوُلَاةِ الْحَقِّ\nILAL I'ZAAMIN NAKHIRATI A'IMMATIL KHALQI WA WULAATIL HAQQ\nto the decayed bones, the Imams of creation and the guardians of the truth.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الشَّخْصُ الشَّرِيْفُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHASH SHAKHSUSH SHAREEF\nPeace be upon you, O noble one,\nاِسْمَاعِيْلُ بْنُ مَوْلَانَا جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ الصَّادِقِ الطَّاهِرِ الْكَرِيْمِ\nISMAA'EELUBNU MAWLAANAA JA'FARIBNI MUHAMMADINIS SAADIQIT TAAHIRIL KAREEM\nIsma'il, son of our master Ja'far son of Muhammad, the truthful, the pure, the generous.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَمُصْطَفَاهُ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WA ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA MUSTAFAAH\nI bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His chosen one,\nوَاَنَّ عَلِيًّا وَلِيُّهٗ وَمُجْتَبَاهُ\nWA ANNA A'LIYYAN WALIYYUHOO WA MUJTABAAH\nand that Ali is His friend and His elect,\nوَاَنَّ الْاِمَامَةَ فِيْ وُلْدِهٖ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الدِّيْنِ\nWA ANNAL IMAAMATA FEE WULDIHEE ILAA YAWMID DEEN\nand that the Imamate is in his descendants until the Day of Judgement.\nنَعْلَمُ ذٰلِكَ عِلْمَ الْيَقِيْنِ\nNA'LAMU DHAALIKA I'LMAL YAQEEN\nWe know this with certain knowledge;\nوَنَحْنُ لِذٰلِكَ مُعْتَقِدُوْنَ وَفِيْ نَصْرِهِمْ مُجْتَهِدُوْنَ\nWA NAHNU LIDHAALIKA MU'TAQIDOONA WA FEE NASRIHIM MUJTAHIDOON\nwe hold it as our faith, and we strive to help them.",
  "merits": "Isma'il was the eldest son of Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.); his mother was Fatimah, daughter of al-Husayn al-Athram, son of Imam al-Hasan (a.s.). His father loved him dearly. He died in his father's lifetime at al-Urayd, near Madinah, and was carried on men's shoulders to al-Baqi (Umdat al-Talib); Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) grieved deeply for him and walked before his bier barefoot (al-Mufid, al-Irshad). The Ismailis take their name from him; this ziyarat affirms the Imamate in the descendants of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.).\n\nIt is given in the Shia manuals of Hajj, such as Sayyid Jawad Husayni Shahrudi's Adab al-Haramayn, without a narrated source."
}
